{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Remark\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Remark</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider sequences of positive real numbers of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/5/a652c9ab7ffac24416e6dc5fac4a32941bfb15f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, 2000, y, \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" /> in which every term after the first is 1 less than the product of its two immediate neighbors. For how many different values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> does the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> appear somewhere in the sequence?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a3806837f3d9d19a818efeb642d10aaaa94ce051.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }1 \\qquad \\text{(B) }2 \\qquad \\text{(C) }3 \\qquad \\text{(D) }4 \\qquad \\text{(E) more than }4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"413\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>It never hurts to compute a few terms of the sequence in order to get a feel how it looks like. In our case, the definition is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536ba5a392431e74fec5a8db2257504c85fcc206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\forall$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"10\" height=\"13\" /> (for all) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bcc9e357d1e635ad9f10b5bca5e3cce93fd6405a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1:~ a_n = a_{n-1}a_{n+1} - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"209\" height=\"16\" />. This can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc4bd8350d840192624db674c85f6474aed0b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = \\frac{a_n +1}{a_{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"111\" height=\"39\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/4753b8e19c22116f74c902bb3a38b1aeb068c8c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/429afc0d55e472d377ad5a1e6ea722559cd4d6f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, and we compute:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02df411113d74be0fea947b10a33e0256db1e49.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_3  &amp; = \\frac{a_2+1}{a_1} = \\frac{2001}x \\\\ a_4  &amp; = \\frac{a_3+1}{a_2} = \\frac{ \\dfrac{2001}x + 1 }{ 2000 } = \\frac{2001 + x}{2000x} \\\\ a_5 &amp; = \\frac{a_4+1}{a_3} = \\frac{ \\frac{2001 + x}{2000x} + 1 }{ \\frac{2001}x } = \\frac{ \\frac{2001 + 2001x}{2000x} }{ \\frac{2001}x } = \\frac{1+x}{2000} \\\\ a_6 &amp; = \\frac{a_5+1}{a_4} = \\frac{ \\frac{1+x}{2000} + 1 }{ \\frac{2001 + x}{2000x} } =  \\frac{ \\frac{2001+x}{2000} }{ \\frac{2001 + x}{2000x} } = x \\\\ a_7 &amp; = \\frac{a_6+1}{a_5} = \\frac{ x+1 }{ \\frac{1+x}{2000} } = 2000 \\end{align*}\" width=\"372\" height=\"262\" />\n</p><p>At this point we see that the sequence will become periodic: we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2f3d4c9868c4815b16f7c73aff9945bc180a98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_6=a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac235c02843c040b03c178e04cb7b79842ef4ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_7=a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, and each subsequent term is uniquely determined by the previous two.\n</p><p>Hence if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> appears, it has to be one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/5/0d5d34d49a7eb6afd4874d7bdaf23946dbf63cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/9/429afc0d55e472d377ad5a1e6ea722559cd4d6f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2=2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, we only have four possibilities left. Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/6/2a64a04c4ad614f76dd717406b4347f480ec18d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813c29120cce09b543f582e90b7e2a1d4f5962f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f023f82b773ee6988219b16da4b78dcbc7093ffe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3=2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c52e02a35db152495396584bfeae1d0599cd753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/4/ab41c501f4fac1760205dfb2ac891ba2d2b3ddec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4=2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d5023f55a7d4086a6efff8b33925db6cf9f3ea7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{2001}{2000\\cdot 2001 - 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"154\" height=\"38\" />, and the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/a/9ea3f3a0cd5fa9c7349994e0f3801c9273289d01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_5=2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc5aaa8696ddc53ec7105ee88d5e0f60955579f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2000\\cdot 2001 - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"150\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>No two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> we just computed are equal, and therefore there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" /> different values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> for which the sequence contains the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7e2da81334aad3aeeb09706fed72248196613b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2001$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Remark\">Remark</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Remark\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In general, notice that the sequence defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c0fd884a9168f9bdec2ed44eaa5087153dbfc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=a, a_2=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc4bd8350d840192624db674c85f6474aed0b0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1} = \\frac{a_n +1}{a_{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"111\" height=\"39\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> is periodic.\n</p><p>~tsun26\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017011219\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 246/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2235/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 133/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6212/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.366      1 -total\n 60.47%    8.082      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 37.75%    5.046      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7845:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017011219 and revision id 231656. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}